From f8c5d4dcf2bc8803ff169cfb299eac470f8ba809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:42:02 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] tests: add SysRoot, a configfs trait and a kernel-rule
 fake

Every path to configfs, sysfs and procfs was a hard-coded constant (plus
two literal /sys/kernel/config strings), and a mode switch read
/proc/device-tree/compatible with `?`, so nothing beyond the pure helpers
could be tested without root, a UDC and a device tree. The configfs
tests are all #[ignore]d and CI never runs them.

- SysRoot { configfs, sysfs, proc } replaces the constants and is passed
  explicitly, so tests point the code at a directory tree. main uses the
  real mount points.
- Systems without a device tree (x86 dummy_hcd test VMs, for example)
  get the serial number "usb-signaller" instead of failing every mode
  switch.
- A small ConfigFs trait covers what recomposing a bound gadget needs:
  mkdir/rmdir of functions, link/unlink, UDC reads and writes, the
  FunctionFS ready attribute and plain attribute writes, with the
  kernel's errno kept in every error. SysConfigFs implements it on the
  real configfs; attribute handles keep configfs' per-open read buffer
  semantics, so fresh reads open a new handle.
- A test-only FakeConfigFs implements the same trait with the kernel's
  rules: no link while a UDC name is set (also after the UDC vanished),
  no cross-gadget links, unlink while bound unbinds, EBUSY for binding
  twice and for every failed bind, ENODEV for unbinding twice, global
  FunctionFS names, no bind with a non-ready FunctionFS function, a
  daemon exit unbinding a bound gadget (deferred with no_disconnect), a
  busy mass storage LUN blocking unbind until forced_eject, rebind when
  the UDC returns, and stale reads through a reused attribute handle.
  Calls are numbered so tests can inject an errno or a concurrent change
  at any step.

New tests cover UDC::load against directory trees (bound gadget through
the function attribute, the scanning fallback, unparseable foreign
gadgets, a gadget without linked functions), set_mode refusing declared,
preserved and broken-config foreign gadgets without writing anything,
the serial fallback, the host role cleanup skipping non-owned gadgets
and continuing past failures, and each fake rule. The #[ignore]d
hardware tests still build and run through scripts/run-tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
